<title>INDIA: Reliance sees 20 pct EPS growth over 5yrs.</title>
<headline>Reliance sees 20 pct EPS growth over 5yrs.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reliance Industries, India's largest private company, has set a 20 percent compound growth target for earnings per share (EPS) over five years, Dhirubhal Ambani, the chairman of the petrochemical and textile company, told the annual general meeting of shareholders in Bombay on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have set ourselves targets of achieving 20 percent compound growth in EPS and a return of 20 percent on shareholders funds over the next five years,&quot; he said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom (91) 22 265 9000</p>
</text>
